/* ========================================================
   pi.kuhul — Reference conformance program for the K'UHUL
   runtime. One small file demonstrating the whole execution
   model: folds, nodes, glyphs, lanes, opcodes, phase
   legality, and provider binding.

   Compile:  python tools/khlc.py drivers/khl/pi.kuhul
   Admit:    python tools/kson_validate.py drivers/khl/pi.kson
   Execute:  KSON loader -> canonical phase engine -> provider

   The phase engine sees the exact Pop -> Wo -> Yax -> Sek
   -> Ch'en -> Xul legality inline — each ⟁ block is a fold.
   ======================================================== */

@bind manifest.pi.config → PI_CONFIG

⟁ Pop ⟁
  bind π = 3.141592653589793
  probe geometry

⟁ Wo ⟁
  bind radius = 8
  bind area = π * radius * radius

⟁ Yax ⟁
  resolve provider = geometry.compute

⟁ Sek ⟁
  dispatch provider(area)

⟁ Ch'en ⟁
  collect_status result

⟁ Xul ⟁
  commit result
